WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:07.680
Jim Morrison, of the 60's rock group The Doors,
was the first rock star to be arrested on

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.639
stage.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:22.690
For one day in 1998, Topeka, Kansas, renamed
itself “ToPikachu” to mark Pokemon's U.S.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:23.980
debut.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.810
The U.S. bought Alaska for 2 cents an acre
from Russia.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:35.370
In the 1700s, "macaroni" was a slang term
for a fashionable man.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.870
98% of people in Japan are cremated.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:46.149
California has issued 6 drivers licenses to
people named “Jesus Christ.”

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:52.120
The top of the Eiffel Tower leans away from
the sun, as the metal facing the sun heats

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.030
up and expands.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.069
It can move as much as 7 inches.

00:00:57.069 --> 00:01:01.909
In 14th-century England, children were baptised
in cider.

00:01:01.909 --> 00:01:06.990
Australian soldiers used the song “We're
Off to See the Wizard” as a marching song

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.600
in WWII.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:17.110
NASA estimates that the near-Earth asteroid,
Eros, contains 20 billion tonnes of gold.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:24.450
During the 17th Century, the Sultan of Turkey
ordered his whole harem of women to be drowned

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.810
and replaced with a new one.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.530
In ancient Egypt, servants were covered in
honey so as to attract flies away from pharaoh.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:40.600
Christmas Day is the number one day for heart
attacks worldwide, followed by December 26th

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.610
and then New Year's Day.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:47.740
The female lion does 90% of the hunting for
the pride.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:56.389
Icelanders consume more Coca-Cola per Capita
than any other nation.

